solnix: tzmon -- ThinkPad discrete-GPU power-off at boot, opt-in (-B solnix-dgpu-off=1), the way Linux powers off
a GPU that no driver owns.

WHY
- Under Pop!_OS the X1 Extreme Gen5's RTX 3080 Ti (10de:2420 at 01:00.0, \_SB.PC00.PEG1.PEGP) runs NVIDIA's runtime
  D3 ("Enabled (fine-grained)"), so the GPU is powered off whenever it is idle. Nothing drives it under illumos, so
  it stays in D0 at full idle power, on a machine whose EC already raises its critical thermal level.
- Linux does the same for a driverless GPU through pci_set_power_state(D3cold): the endpoint to D3hot through its PM
  capability, then the root port's D3 power resource (_PR3) off, which the platform implements as link-down, reset
  and power-cut.

WHERE IT LIVES: in tzmon's ThinkPad shim, not a separate pseudo driver.
- The gate is the same ThinkPad HKEY that 0002 already finds (tzmon_hkey), and it must run once at boot, before
  devfsadm, on a node that is force-attached early. tzmon is that node (tzmon.conf ddi-forceattach=1).
- A separate driver would need its own .conf, name_to_major entry and force-attach, all for one function.

WHAT THE X1E'S TABLES SAY (BIOS N3JET48W, SSDT14 "NvOptTbl", solnix-bank/evidence/x1e-acpi-N3JET48W/ssdt/SSDT14.dsl)
- \_SB.PC00.PEG1 has _PR0 = _PR3 = { PXP } (lines 550-557). Linux lists it as \_SB_.PC00.PEG1.PXP_ (LNXPOWER:01).
- PXP._OFF (lines 525-547) acts when OSYS > 0x07D9; illumos's _OSI answers make OSYS 0x07DF. It runs GC6I if
  PEGP.TDGC is 1, which only NVIDIA's _DSM (NGC6) sets; otherwise it runs POFF().
- POFF (lines 433-494):
  - returns early if the port has no device (RPVD 0xFFFF) or the power GPIO is already off;
  - NVPF saves the link state;
  - PEG1.DL23 puts the link in L2/L3 ready, because PEGP.OTMS is 0 unless PEGP._PS3 ran with OMPR == 3 (lines
    896-913);
  - the clock request is dropped (SPCO);
  - \PIN.ON(RSTG) asserts the GPU reset, and \PIN.OFF(PWRG) cuts its power.
- So with no NVIDIA driver loaded, PXP._OFF needs NO _DSM handshake.
- After it, config reads of 01:00.x return all 1s, and nothing may touch the device again.

THE SEQUENCE (tzmon_dgpu_off, called from tzmon_attach right after the HKEY init)
1. Do nothing unless the boot property solnix-dgpu-off is set and non-zero (string from -B, or int from tzmon.conf).
2. Gate:
   - the ThinkPad HKEY (tzmon_hkey != NULL);
   - \_SB.PC00.PEG1, or \_SB.PCI0.PEG1 on older ThinkPads;
   - the port's _PR3 package naming a PowerResource object.
   Otherwise log "not a ThinkPad dGPU (...)" and do nothing. On EC2 (no HKEY) that is the only effect.
3. Walk the root port's devinfo children (acpica tags PCI nodes with their ACPI device at boot). Any child with an
   attached driver is in use, so log it and do nothing.
4. Read the power resource's _STA. If it is 0 (already off), do nothing.
5. ndi_devi_offline every function, so devfsadm and later configuration never attach vgatext/audiohd to a function
   whose power is about to go. If any function refuses to go offline, stop there with the GPU still powered.
6. Put every function in D3hot through its PCI PM capability (PMCSR), wait 10 ms (PCIe D0 -> D3hot), and read back
   the state.
7. Evaluate the power resource's _OFF, then its _STA.
8. One console line: the port, the number of functions, the D3hot result, and _STA before -> after.
After step 7 nothing reads or writes the GPU's config space.

RUNG REACHED (this patch)
- compiles with gcc 10 -Wall -Wextra -Werror;
- 0 unresolved symbols against kernel-nd's unix + genunix + misc/acpica, apart from the SDT probes krtld resolves;
- loads on the solnix DP AMI (EC2, no HKEY): with the property it logs "not a ThinkPad dGPU (no HKEY)", without it
  stays silent;
- under KVM with an SSDT that defines HKEY + PEG1 + _PR3 = { PXP } and a PXP._OFF that writes a marker, _OFF runs
  exactly once with the flag and never without it.
NOT run on the X1E itself. Default off.
--- a/usr/src/uts/i86pc/io/tzmon/tzmon.c	2026-10-20 20:11:31.708790867 -0400
+++ b/usr/src/uts/i86pc/io/tzmon/tzmon.c	2026-10-20 20:11:31.727629244 -0400
@@ -42,6 +42,10 @@
 #include <sys/acpica.h>
 #include <sys/sdt.h>
 #include <sys/kstat.h>
+#include <sys/pci.h>
+#include <sys/pci_cfgspace.h>
+#include <sys/sunndi.h>
+#include <sys/ddi_implfuncs.h>
 
 #include "tzmon.h"
 
@@ -94,6 +98,7 @@
 static void tzmon_hkey_disable(void);
 static void tzmon_kstat_create(thermal_zone_t *tzp, int instance);
 static void tzmon_ec_temps(int *t, int *l);
+static void tzmon_dgpu_off(dev_info_t *dip);
 
 extern void halt(char *);
 
@@ -202,6 +207,8 @@
 
 	/* before the zones are first evaluated; see tzmon_hkey_enable() */
 	tzmon_hkey_enable();
+	/* opt-in only (boot property solnix-dgpu-off); see tzmon_dgpu_off() */
+	tzmon_dgpu_off(dip);
 	tzmon_find_zones();
 	mutex_enter(&zone_list_lock);
 	if (zone_count < 1) {
@@ -1049,3 +1056,202 @@
 	    tzmon_hkey_notify);
 	tzmon_hkey = NULL;
 }
+
+
+/*
+ * ThinkPad discrete-GPU power-off at boot, opt-in with -B solnix-dgpu-off=1.
+ *
+ * Under Linux the X1 Extreme Gen5's RTX 3080 Ti runs NVIDIA's runtime D3
+ * (fine-grained): the GPU is powered off whenever it is idle. Nothing drives
+ * it under illumos, so it stays in D0 at full idle power, which is extra heat
+ * on a machine that already reaches the EC's critical level. This does what
+ * Linux's pci_set_power_state(D3cold) does for a GPU with no driver: put the
+ * endpoint in D3hot through its PCI PM capability, then turn off the root
+ * port's D3 power resource (its _PR3) so the platform cuts the GPU's power.
+ *
+ * The X1E's tables (BIOS N3JET48W, SSDT14 "NvOptTbl"): \_SB.PC00.PEG1 has
+ * _PR0 = _PR3 = { PXP } (SSDT14.dsl lines 550-557). PXP._OFF (lines 525-547)
+ * runs POFF() (lines 433-494) unless PEGP.TDGC is set, and only the NVIDIA
+ * _DSM sets TDGC. POFF returns early if the port is empty or already off,
+ * then saves link state (NVPF), puts the link in L2/L3 ready (PEG1.DL23),
+ * drops the clock request, asserts the GPU reset GPIO and cuts its power GPIO.
+ * With no NVIDIA driver loaded, that needs no _DSM handshake. After it, the
+ * GPU's config space reads all 1s, so nothing here touches it again, and the
+ * functions are offlined first so devfsadm never attaches a driver to them.
+ *
+ * Gates: the boot property, the ThinkPad HKEY (tzmon_hkey), and a PEG1
+ * device whose _PR3 names a power resource. Anything else logs one line and
+ * does nothing.
+ */
+static char *tzmon_dgpu_ports[] = { "\\_SB.PC00.PEG1", "\\_SB.PCI0.PEG1",
+	NULL };
+
+typedef struct tzmon_dgpu_fn {
+	dev_info_t	*dip;
+	int		bus, dev, func;
+} tzmon_dgpu_fn_t;
+
+/* Put one function in D3hot via its PCI PM capability; -1 if it has none. */
+static int
+tzmon_dgpu_d3hot(tzmon_dgpu_fn_t *fn)
+{
+	uint8_t ptr;
+	uint16_t pmcsr;
+	int n;
+
+	if (!((*pci_getw_func)(fn->bus, fn->dev, fn->func, PCI_CONF_STAT) &
+	    PCI_STAT_CAP))
+		return (-1);
+	ptr = (*pci_getb_func)(fn->bus, fn->dev, fn->func, PCI_CONF_CAP_PTR);
+	for (n = 0; ptr >= 0x40 && n < 48; n++) {
+		ptr &= ~3;
+		if ((*pci_getb_func)(fn->bus, fn->dev, fn->func, ptr) ==
+		    PCI_CAP_ID_PM)
+			break;
+		ptr = (*pci_getb_func)(fn->bus, fn->dev, fn->func, ptr + 1);
+	}
+	if (ptr < 0x40 || n >= 48)
+		return (-1);
+	pmcsr = (*pci_getw_func)(fn->bus, fn->dev, fn->func, ptr + PCI_PMCSR);
+	pmcsr = (pmcsr & ~PCI_PMCSR_STATE_MASK) | PCI_PMCSR_D3HOT;
+	(*pci_putw_func)(fn->bus, fn->dev, fn->func, ptr + PCI_PMCSR, pmcsr);
+	/* PCIe: 10 ms from D0 to D3hot before the next access */
+	delay(drv_usectohz(10000));
+	pmcsr = (*pci_getw_func)(fn->bus, fn->dev, fn->func, ptr + PCI_PMCSR);
+	return (pmcsr & PCI_PMCSR_STATE_MASK);
+}
+
+/*
+ * The opt-in: -B solnix-dgpu-off=1 (a boot property: a string) or
+ * solnix-dgpu-off=1; in tzmon.conf (an int). Looked up from tzmon's node up
+ * to the root node, so either works.
+ */
+static int
+tzmon_dgpu_wanted(dev_info_t *dip)
+{
+	char *s;
+	int v;
+
+	if (ddi_prop_lookup_string(DDI_DEV_T_ANY, dip, 0, "solnix-dgpu-off",
+	    &s) == DDI_PROP_SUCCESS) {
+		v = (s[0] != '\0' && strcmp(s, "0") != 0);
+		ddi_prop_free(s);
+		return (v);
+	}
+	return (ddi_prop_get_int(DDI_DEV_T_ANY, dip, 0, "solnix-dgpu-off",
+	    0) != 0);
+}
+
+static void
+tzmon_dgpu_off(dev_info_t *dip)
+{
+	ACPI_HANDLE port = NULL, pr = NULL;
+	ACPI_BUFFER rb;
+	ACPI_OBJECT *pkg;
+	dev_info_t *pdip = NULL, *cdip;
+	tzmon_dgpu_fn_t fn[8];
+	char *name = NULL;
+	int nfn = 0, sta0 = -1, sta1 = -1, i, d3[8];
+	ACPI_OBJECT_TYPE t;
+
+	if (!tzmon_dgpu_wanted(dip))
+		return;
+
+	for (i = 0; tzmon_dgpu_ports[i] != NULL && port == NULL; i++) {
+		if (AcpiGetHandle(NULL, tzmon_dgpu_ports[i], &port) != AE_OK)
+			port = NULL;
+		else
+			name = tzmon_dgpu_ports[i];
+	}
+	if (tzmon_hkey == NULL || port == NULL) {
+		cmn_err(CE_NOTE, "tzmon: solnix-dgpu-off: not a ThinkPad dGPU "
+		    "(%s); nothing done", tzmon_hkey == NULL ? "no HKEY" :
+		    "no PEG1 root port");
+		return;
+	}
+
+	/* the D3 power resource: the first entry of the port's _PR3 */
+	rb.Length = ACPI_ALLOCATE_BUFFER;
+	rb.Pointer = NULL;
+	if (AcpiEvaluateObjectTyped(port, "_PR3", NULL, &rb,
+	    ACPI_TYPE_PACKAGE) == AE_OK) {
+		pkg = rb.Pointer;
+		if (pkg->Package.Count >= 1 &&
+		    pkg->Package.Elements[0].Type == ACPI_TYPE_LOCAL_REFERENCE &&
+		    AcpiGetType(pkg->Package.Elements[0].Reference.Handle,
+		    &t) == AE_OK && t == ACPI_TYPE_POWER)
+			pr = pkg->Package.Elements[0].Reference.Handle;
+		AcpiOsFree(rb.Pointer);
+	}
+	if (pr == NULL) {
+		cmn_err(CE_NOTE, "tzmon: solnix-dgpu-off: not a ThinkPad dGPU "
+		    "(%s has no _PR3 power resource); nothing done", name);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * The GPU's functions: the PCI children of the root port's devinfo
+	 * node (acpica tags PCI nodes with their ACPI device at boot). Any
+	 * attached driver means hands off: the device is in use.
+	 */
+	if (acpica_get_devinfo(port, &pdip) != AE_OK || pdip == NULL) {
+		cmn_err(CE_NOTE, "tzmon: solnix-dgpu-off: %s has no devinfo "
+		    "node; nothing done", name);
+		return;
+	}
+	ndi_devi_enter(pdip);
+	for (cdip = ddi_get_child(pdip); cdip != NULL && nfn < 8;
+	    cdip = ddi_get_next_sibling(cdip)) {
+		if (acpica_get_bdf(cdip, &fn[nfn].bus, &fn[nfn].dev,
+		    &fn[nfn].func) < 0)
+			continue;
+		if (i_ddi_devi_attached(cdip)) {
+			ndi_devi_exit(pdip);
+			cmn_err(CE_NOTE, "tzmon: solnix-dgpu-off: %s@%x,%x has "
+			    "a driver (%s); nothing done", ddi_node_name(cdip),
+			    fn[nfn].dev, fn[nfn].func,
+			    ddi_driver_name(cdip));
+			return;
+		}
+		fn[nfn++].dip = cdip;
+	}
+	ndi_devi_exit(pdip);
+	if (nfn == 0) {
+		cmn_err(CE_NOTE, "tzmon: solnix-dgpu-off: %s has no device; "
+		    "nothing done", name);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	(void) acpica_eval_int(pr, "_STA", &sta0);
+	if (sta0 == 0) {
+		cmn_err(CE_NOTE, "tzmon: solnix-dgpu-off: %s _PR3 power "
+		    "resource already off (_STA 0); nothing done", name);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * Offline every function first, so no driver attaches later. A
+	 * function that will not go offline could still get a driver, which
+	 * would then touch a powered-off device: stop before any change.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < nfn; i++) {
+		if (ndi_devi_offline(fn[i].dip, 0) != NDI_SUCCESS) {
+			cmn_err(CE_NOTE, "tzmon: solnix-dgpu-off: %s@%x,%x "
+			    "would not go offline; GPU left powered",
+			    ddi_node_name(fn[i].dip), fn[i].dev, fn[i].func);
+			return;
+		}
+	}
+	for (i = 0; i < nfn; i++)
+		d3[i] = tzmon_dgpu_d3hot(&fn[i]);
+
+	/* then the power resource; nothing touches the GPU after this */
+	(void) AcpiEvaluateObject(pr, "_OFF", NULL, NULL);
+	(void) acpica_eval_int(pr, "_STA", &sta1);
+
+	cmn_err(CE_NOTE, "tzmon: solnix-dgpu-off: %s: %d function(s) at "
+	    "bus %d dev %d offlined, PM state %d%s; _PR3 _OFF evaluated, "
+	    "_STA %d -> %d", name, nfn, fn[0].bus, fn[0].dev, d3[0],
+	    (d3[0] == PCI_PMCSR_D3HOT) ? " (D3hot)" : (d3[0] < 0 ?
+	    " (no PM capability)" : " (D3hot not reached)"), sta0, sta1);
+}
